For mechanical convergent work — making a failing suite green, migrating call sites —
use a bounded loop rather than one long attempt:

    ilk dev-loops run 'your-agent-command'

Two rules make it safe. **State lives in the repository**, so progress survives a
context window ending; nothing important may live only in the conversation. And
**completion is decided by `{{ .Vars.gate }}`, never by the model's own assessment** —
the loop stops when the gate passes or after {{ .Vars.max_iterations }} attempts,
whichever comes first.

A loop that hits its ceiling is a finding, not a failure to try harder. Report what it
converged on and what it did not.
